WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.325
Why should a modernization
program care about meeting habits?

2
00:00:03.325 --> 00:00:06.725
Because meetings are where the
program is actually coordinated.

3
00:00:06.725 --> 00:00:11.211
From the change advisory board to the
cutover go or no-go call to the steering

4
00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:15.625
committee, most of the program's decisions
get made in a meeting of some kind.

5
00:00:15.625 --> 00:00:19.302
And the guide makes a sharper
point: most of a program's slippage

6
00:00:19.302 --> 00:00:23.475
starts in a meeting that ended without
a clear decision or a named owner.

7
00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:26.400
So a meeting that drifts
isn't just a lost hour.

8
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.038
It can be the moment a schedule starts to
slip, with nobody holding the next step.

9
00:00:31.038 --> 00:00:33.500
The good news is that the fix isn't new.
